    "\n",
    "# BGM rebuttal experiment: exact 3D Gaussian--OT + CIFAR-100 pixel pilot\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook is designed for the NeurIPS rebuttal/revision concern:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. empirical validation is narrow,\n",
    "2. image results are feature-space proxies,\n",
    "3. the Markovization gap might only measure transport cost,\n",
    "4. the refined object should be \\(\\mathfrak G(\\mathscr Q,U,\\mathcal O)\\), not only \\(\\mathfrak G(\\mathscr Q)\\).\n",
    "\n",
    "The notebook has two parts.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Part A: exact 3D Euclidean Gaussian--OT diagnostic.**  This runs on CPU, needs no neural network and no kNN/PCA proxy. It computes the exact gap from Gaussian conditional covariance. It varies coupling, bridge law, and sampler-visible state.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Part B: CIFAR-100 larger-dataset pilot.**  This is a GPU-capable, low-compute pixel-space flow-matching pilot. It estimates a pre-training feature-space proxy gap on CIFAR-100, trains independent vs minibatch-OT straight-bridge models under matched compute, and optionally computes FID/KID/IS.\n",
    "\n",
    "Important interpretation: the image proxy gap is a **feature-space screening score**, not a certified estimate of the high-dimensional population gap. The exact 3D experiment is the clean control showing that the theoretical gap is not reducible to endpoint cost or path length.\n"
   ]
  },
