    "\n",
    "## Interpretation for rebuttal\n",
    "\n",
    "Use the following distinction.\n",
    "\n",
    "The raw proxy gap is an **absolute regression burden**. It is expected to track flow-matching training loss because the loss is an absolute squared-error objective.\n",
    "\n",
    "The normalized ratio \\(\\eta\\) is a **relative unexplained-variance fraction**. It asks whether the Markov state explains a larger fraction of the velocity variance. This ratio may move differently from the raw gap. If OT reduces raw gap but increases or does not improve \\(\\eta\\), the correct interpretation is that OT reduces the absolute burden largely through shorter/lower-energy endpoint transport. That is still useful for training, but it is not evidence of transport-cost-free conditional ambiguity reduction.\n",
    "\n",
    "Therefore, for rebuttal, lead with the exact 3D Gaussian--OT control when answering whether the theoretical Markovization gap is more than transport cost. Use CIFAR-100/CIFAR-10/Fashion-MNIST proxies only as practical within-dataset ranking diagnostics.\n"
   ]
